# Constants and Config Source of Truth

- Never read Python source text with regex/string parsing to extract constants or configuration values.
- Never infer runtime constants by scraping implementation files.

Allowed approaches:
- Use constants defined in this project under `environment_definition.constants`.
- Use explicit exported constants/API from dependencies (for example, a dedicated constants module).
- If dependency constants are not exported cleanly, ask for a proper adapter/config decision instead of scraping files.

When integrating external libraries:
- Keep project-facing constants owned by this repository unless the user explicitly requests dependency-owned constants.
- Prefer explicit mapping functions between project constants and dependency config objects.

Bad pattern (forbidden):
- `read_text(...)` + regex to extract `GM_Earth`, `R_Earth`, etc. from dependency source files.
